/-
  OIBridge/MicroscopicReversibility.lean — the primitive-source audit, third target: the
  inverse clause of reversible richness, derived from dagger-stable implementations.

  ROUND FIFTY-EIGHT. After round fifty-seven the carrier-general quantum-complete package is
  implementation locality, reversible richness and embedded observation. Reversible richness
  is a conjunction of two different things, and the audit treats them separately:

      · INVERSE ACCESSIBILITY (`InverseAccessibility`) — every available conjugation channel
        has its adjoint channel available;
      · LIE-RANK RICHNESS (`LieRankRichness`) — at every level, a self-adjoint drift with
        finitely many unitary controls whose control Lie algebra contains `su(D)`, with the
        flows and the controls available.

  `reversibleRichness_iff` records that reversible richness is exactly their conjunction.

  THE REDUNDANCY TEST. Implementation locality, embedded observation and Lie-rank richness
  force inverse accessibility: Lie-rank richness alone gives full composite unitary control
  (`control_of_lieRank`, from the positive-reachability theorem
  `universalReachability_of_lieRank_positive`, which consumes no inverse of a control), and on
  a well-formed theory full control yields the inverse clause
  (`inverseAccessibility_of_lieRank`). The round-50 reachability theorem with the `hstar`
  hypothesis (`control_of_lieRank_inverse`) is kept as the place where the clause was consumed.
  The file also derives the clause from a primitive below availability.

  THE PRIMITIVE, BELOW AVAILABILITY. An implementation class is DAGGER-STABLE when the
  adjoint of an admissible operator is admissible: `𝓘 S K → 𝓘 S Kᴴ` (`DaggerStable`).
  This is closure of elementary implementation amplitudes under reversal; it mentions no
  availability. `ReversibleImplementationLocality` is implementation locality with a
  dagger-stable class.

  THE DERIVATION. If a conjugation channel `conj V` is available and the theory is
  implementation-generated by an architecture, then `conj V = ∑ conj (K i)` with admissible
  `K i` (`realized_of_instAvail`), and the aggregate trace makes `V` an isometry. The Choi
  matrix of `conj V` is the dyad of the vectorized `V`, so the dyads of the `K i` sum to a
  rank-one dyad and every `K i` lies on the ray of `V` (`dyad_sum_span_single`,
  `kraus_of_conj_unitary`): `K i = c i • V`, and some `c i` is nonzero
  (`exists_scaled_mem_of_instAvail_unitary`). The adjoint of a protocol is not a protocol, so
  the unitary itself has to be admissible: UNITARY-RAY SATURATION (`UnitaryRaySaturated`), a
  class containing a nonzero scalar multiple of a unitary contains the unitary, lifts `c i • V`
  to `V`, dagger stability supplies `Vᴴ`, and one step realizes `conj Vᴴ`. Hence
  `inverseAccessibility_of_generated_daggerStable`, for an architecture that is dagger-stable
  and unitary-ray saturated. Saturation is a statement about admissible operators, not about
  the phase resource of a theory; it enters at this one place and in no package. No
  Kraus-uniqueness theorem is invoked; the rank-one specialization is an elementary span lemma
  in the style of `dyad_sum_span`.

  NECESSITY. Exact finite operational QM is generated by the full class, which is
  dagger-stable (`reversibleImplementationLocality_of_qm`).

  THE COMPRESSED SET. `OIPlusMicro` is reversible implementation locality, Lie-rank richness
  and embedded observation; `carrier_general_oiPlusMicro` proves it equivalent to exact
  finite endomorphic operational QM on every nonempty finite carrier, the inverse clause
  taken from Lie-rank control on the well-formed theory, so that neither dagger stability nor
  saturation is consumed by the equivalence. The Lie-rank clause is the one substantive
  selector whose source is not audited here.

  WHAT IS NOT CLAIMED. The converse from inverse accessibility to dagger stability. That
  inverse accessibility follows from dagger stability without saturation. Any source for the
  Lie-rank clause.
-/

